<title>USA: TABLE - Bank of Oklahoma sells $150 mln notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Bank of Oklahoma sells $150 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Bank of Oklahoma was priced on Wednesday, according to joint-lead manager Bear Stearns &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>Chase Securities was the other manager on the deal.</p>
<p>BORROWER BANK OF OKLAHOMA</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 7.125 PCT  MATURITY 8/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SUB NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.478  FIRST PAY DATE 2/15/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA3  YIELD  7.199 PCT  PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD +83 BPS    CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((Caryn Trokie, U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
